  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8ef4a382a350f98438c21cfd3c789fdf, type: 3}
  m_Name: DoubleThreat
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonTitle: Double Threat
  lessonId: doublethreat
  slides:
  - slideName: Slide 1
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: In this lesson, you will learn about the "double threat", an easy capturing
      technique.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 2
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Take a look at the two highlighted white stones. Notice how they both
      only have two liberties left and are only one grid away from each other?
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 3
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: When black plays at the lighlighted spot, both stones are put in Atari.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 4
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: White can only save one while black takes the other. This is called
      the double threat because two stones (or groups of stones) are put in Atari
      in one move.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 5
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: This is another reason why a failed laddering attempt is so dangerous.
      See how in this example, black failed such attempt and is left with this many
      spots where white can perform double threats.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 6
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Now it's your turn. Perform a double threat on white!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 0c5b3636391ec4e48843a4b41d9d23be, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 7
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Perform a double threat on white!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 59c8eab87a166684b9ec29b7ac02d115, type: 3}
